-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Hard Drivin'
  Publisher   Domark, 1989
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        hd.tap
  MD5         02e1f96c6b0b872859283b16f761c3b6

  File        hd.tzx
  MD5         61f7d04c538e35029ca909e77f82f682

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. The menu's Finer time steps line adds more; see the note. Game
  logic is changed: each update is split into 2 to 4 finer time steps, with
  manual gears gated to one shift an update as the original (the menu's
  Original time steps line gives the original back).

  Pace        slowdown removed

  Changes     1.1: faster (hardware multiply, DMA view copy), manual-gear fix,
              heading smoothing (menu toggle), core 3.03
              1.0: first NXC patch, for the tape, from nexclash hard_drivin
              (steps route + loading screen; toggle: the smooth route)

  Note        Keys as the original. Finer time steps: each game update is
              split into 2 to 4 sub-steps run at 28 MHz and paced to real time
              (one race-clock second a second), so the car reads the controls
              and the 3D view is drawn 2 to 4 times as often; a held gear key
              shifts once an update, as the original. Heading smoothing
              (default): during a turn the 3D view's objects and road move in
              smaller steps between the game's heading steps (display only;
              the mountain backdrop still steps). The picture stays the
              original's: no sprites, the same colours. The loading screen
              (the tape has none; supplied by the owner) shows from ENTER
              while the patch builds and the game loads. Toggles: No heading
              smoothing draws the view at the game's own heading, as the
              original; Original time steps plays the original's own update
              steps at its own pace, with in-between views of the 3D scene
              drawn at 28 MHz for a smoother picture (it has no heading
              smoothing, so the two are never on together).

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite time
   2  Hard pilot
   3  9 replays
   4  Infinite off-road
   5  No crashes

  Cheats are the archive's POKEs (The Tipshop: Gerard Sweeney, Hippy Smith),
  checked against this release. Each was read in the game's code and run in
  the NexClash simulator; easy steering left out.

