-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Phase 1 .nex builds (the steps build with and without the
              loading screen, and without heading smoothing) played by the
              owner on a Spectrum Next, core 3.03, 2026-11-24: "work great";
              this patch through the real loader not yet played

  Replay      1.1 (2026-11-24, nexclash hard_drivin route 2a phase 1, branch
              hd-phase1; auto PASSED, stamped selftest --verify PASSED): the
              owner's recording, 22,116 frames, 1,555 updates. Steps build:
              each update run by the build's model (sub-steps at 28 MHz, the
              Next's paging, Z80N MUL, zxnDMA) and by an independent spec of
              the sub-step rules from the same state, adaptive N and fixed N =
              1 / 2 / 4: 6,220 cases, 0 mismatches (N = 1 also equals the
              recording); the multiplies tested exhaustively, the DMA view
              copy and the gear gate by unit tests; 27 of 27 negative controls
              caught; model pace per update 10.00 / 10.02 / 10.70 frames
              (median / p95 / max; 10 = real time). No heading smoothing
              (display only): game logic IDENTICAL with it on: the spec with
              and without the smoothing from the same recorded states, 90 runs
              of 20 updates at N = 1 / 2 / 4, all 128K outside the render's
              own view bytes and every register but those the view copy loads
              from them equal, 3,676 smoothed views, 0 fail; on all 1,552
              updates every byte it changes is one the render writes and the
              logic never reads. Its layer: the build equals the spec byte for
              byte with the view (smoothing on), and with bl_on 0 equals the
              spec without it; looked at in JNext on a slow turn. Original
              time steps: 3,112 checks of the real update and 3,281 in-between
              views, 0 fail. ROM paths: every byte the game runs is as
              recorded.

  Emulator    JNext: the phase 1 steps build, 9,000 frames with and without
              heading smoothing: update 10.00 frames median, 0 views early;
              screenshots of a slow turn compared (objects and road edges a
              pixel or two apart, the backdrop unchanged). 1.0: 120 race-clock
              seconds in 120.12 s. This patch's build not run in JNext.

  Coverage    The owner's recording of play from the title screen (22,116
              frames). Not covered: stopwatch against the race clock on
              hardware for phase 1, race end and the replay menus, 9 replays
              and No crashes on recorded play (synthetic states only), the
              gear fix on recorded play (synthetic held keys), joystick.

  Hardware    Spectrum Next, core 3.03, played by the owner 2026-11-24: the
              phase 1 .nex builds (the steps build with and without the
              loading screen, and without heading smoothing) "work great";
              2026-11-23: the steps build "plays much better", the smooth
              build plays like the original. This patch (through the real
              loader, its toggles and trainers) not yet run on hardware.

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
